Decode the eap and active_account identity claims.

What: loads() and from_unverified_jwt() now read eap and active_account
(standing, member block, validity). valid keeps absent/null (None), false and
true apart via a new _optional_bool helper. Wrong JSON types raise
IdentityDecodeError like every other field.

Files: iam/_wire.py, tests/test_wire.py.

Why: decode ignored the claims, so loads-then-dumps dropped them and every
downstream service lost the credit verdict and EAP flag. The forwarding test
round-trips all five captured fixtures byte for byte.

Checks: make check (869 tests); independent review approved. Noted, not
changed: nanos/seconds are not range-checked to int32/int64, same as the
existing seat fields.
